      "summaries": {
        "en": "Apollo-11 is the original source code for the Apollo 11 Guidance Computer (AGC), providing a rare historical artifact that demonstrates how early computing solved critical spaceflight challenges. It's written entirely in Assembly language, showcasing how engineers optimized limited hardware through meticulous low-level programming to control spacecraft navigation and landing. Developers can study this code to understand historical software engineering techniques, simulate the AGC's operations, or create educational tools that bring computing history to life.",
        "zh": "Apollo-11项目保存了阿波罗11号制导计算机（AGC）的原始源代码，这是早期计算技术解决关键航天问题的珍贵历史记录。该代码完全用汇编语言编写，展示了工程师如何通过精密的底层编程在有限硬件上实现航天器导航和着陆控制，体现了极致的性能优化思想。开发者可以研究这些代码学习历史软件工程方法，模拟AGC的运行逻辑，或创建教育工具来重现这段计算历史，从中获得对现代系统设计的启发。",
        "es": "Apollo-11 is the original source code for the Apollo 11 Guidance Computer (AGC), providing a rare historical artifact that demonstrates how early computing solved critical spaceflight challenges. It's written entirely in Assembly language, showcasing how engineers optimized limited hardware through meticulous low-level programming to control spacecraft navigation and landing. Developers can study this code to understand historical software engineering techniques, simulate the AGC's operations, or create educational tools that bring computing history to life.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "Apollo-11 stands out for agc, apollo, and hacktoberfest in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Apollo-11 is the original source code for the Apollo 11 Guidance Computer (AGC), providing a rare historical artifact that demonstrates how early computing solved critical spaceflight challenges. It's written entirely in Assembly language, showcasing how engineers optimized limited hardware through meticulous low-level programming to control spacecraft navigation and landing. Developers can study this code to understand historical software engineering techniques, simulate the AGC's operations, or create educational tools that bring computing history to life.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/chrislgarry/Apollo-11 for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
